FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/bytecode/vm.rs:941 — nested `object` panics on `.take().expect("an object declaration being assembled")` — the tree-walking VM explicitly supports a nested `object` in the body (src/vm.rs:1041 runs `rest` after registration so it may extend the enclosing type), but the bytecode VM keeps a single `pending_object: Option` overwritten at def_object (src/bytecode/vm.rs:1776), so the inner unwind takes the inner pending to None and the outer unwind panics instead of erroring — keep a stack of pendings or reject nesting with a clean Error.
2. [MAJOR] tests/common/vm.rs:84 — `tree_walk_verbose` discards the Ok value with `result.err()` and `tree_walk` (tests/common/vm.rs:111) re-lexes, re-parses and re-runs the whole program to recover it — every corpus/generated comparison executes impure programs twice (double `say`/file/time side effects, double cost) and the recovery path uses `.expect()` panics instead of Errors — return the value from the first pipeline instead of re-running it.
3. [MAJOR] tests/common/generator.rs:327 — `loop_forms` emits `"set xs = []\n"`, checked in as corpus/loop-forms-0017.rb with `#label LexerError` — a family that claims to pin loop forms holds a malformed program, inflating the loop count while testing no loop — replace it with a real loop form or move it to `malformed`.
4. [MINOR] tests/common/corpus.rs:68 — `corpus()` uses `.filter_map(|entry| entry.ok())`, silently dropping unreadable directory entries — a shrinking/corrupt corpus entry is hidden instead of reported — propagate the IO error or panic naming the directory.
5. [MINOR] tests/common/generator.rs:581 — doc comment says "The five failures" but `FAULTS` holds six entries — count drift between docs and the list the coverage assertion pins — change the comment to six.
6. [STYLE] src/bytecode/codegen.rs:155 — the `is_last` doc sentence is duplicated verbatim across lines 152-157 — copy-paste that confuses the value-bearing contract — delete one copy.
